## Findings

- **Why the trunk rendered green**: the textured branch of `props_ps.hlsl` is `albedo = lerp(1, Tint, tintable) * tex.rgb` with `tintable = all(PartColor channels) >= 0.99` — white trunk verts (round 2's "brown comes from the sprite" intent) still get the biome tint multiplied in. PartColor is otherwise ignored in the textured branch, so any value <0.99 disables tinting; trunk is now solid brown, leaves keep biome tint (intended).
- UV convention confirmed end-to-end: V=0 = image top row, no flip (same as grass cards).
- Budget: measured tri save from cardCount 6→5 was ~96, not the "~240" the task string estimated; final 2928/2932/2955/2940 ≤3000 (worst case 3044), DECIDUOUS_FAR 68, validateMesh PASS, crown max r 0.599 < 0.80 lateral cap (no clamping), 0 mixed-uv tris, cards within 0.125 of a branch.
- Data pipeline gotcha: after touching anything under `c-game/data`, you must repack with `cd c-game && BIN_DIR=$(pwd)/../build/c-game bash ../scripts/data.sh` — the game loads `build/c-game/data/pak_*.pak` zips.
- Crown-width lever: the 48° trunk forks (lev[0]) set crown width; the 70/55° tweaks moved it <2%. If it still reads too wide: L1 angle 70→60 or L1 length 0.30→0.26.
- Visuals: /tmp/tree-verify3.jpg + /tmp/zoom3_tree.jpg — thin brown trunk, high fork, leaflet-cluster crown matching the reference style; no halos at alphaTest 0.5; cutout shadows work. First sprite pass (7 big leaflets) read as flat oval leaves — the 15-small-leaflet sprite fixed that.
- Cosmetic leftovers: crown radius 0.43–0.60 vs reference ~0.35–0.40; trunk tan vs greener-gray reference bark (both one-knob tweaks in the sprite script); per-variant low drooping clumps (~0.3H) which the reference also exhibits.

